From 672405f2872eb6edfa9cf1508c3a5b1eb8c2a1a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: issakakar <Issakakar@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:44:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] fix(editor): make the query path safe against re-entry
 and reuse

Two latent bugs, both from a query outliving the search that filled it.

getShapeAtPoint kept a single query on the editor and read it across
opts.filter and getShapeGeometry, which are user code. A nested
getShapeAtPoint from either would have run a search into the same membership
and the outer call would have picked the wrong shape. It now takes one from
the pool and releases it in a finally.

release() zeroed the size but left the membership behind, so a pooled query
handed to a second caller answered has() from the first caller's search until
it ran one of its own. It now answers nothing until searched.

Also exports ShapeSpatialIndex and SpatialQuery from the package entry, since
SpatialIndexManager's signatures reference them, and reaches the index through
getSpatialIndex() rather than a getter, which the repo's lint rule disallows.
